{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CKXujFxfG8ctmdPAbb19RN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and determine what to build next.\n\n## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThe project is `go-unix-utils`, a specification-driven regeneration of Unix utilities in Go. The pipeline is: extract specs from C source → specify (PRD + use case) → synthesize (AI generates Go code) → verify (differential testing against GNU reference binaries).\n\n## Step 2: Summarize Project State\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge from reference behavior on edge cases. This project uses GNU utilities as a stress test for an AI code generation system (mage-claude-orchestrator).\n\n\nThe codebase is organized into command packages, testing infrastructure, syscall abstractions, and output formatting utilities, with build targets and documentation. Specifications exist for the core support packages, but implementation coverage varies across the individual utilities.\n\nLooking at what's actually implemented versus what's still needed: I have working code for ts, cat, and the testing framework, but wc tests, sponge, and the sys/format packages are still missing, along with ls and du entirely. The current release is focused on ts with its specification and differential testing approach. Looking at the implementation status more carefully, the ts command shows code exists but is marked as \"implementation pending\" — this suggests the generated code hasn't been verified or tested yet. Since rel01.0 is the earliest incomplete release and contains only ts, I should focus on validating and completing that before moving to other tasks. task).\n\nWhat's missing? Let me think about what would be the highest priority single task.\n\nLooking at rel01.0:\n- pkg/testutils has code\n- cmd/ts has code (main.go and ts_test.go)\n\nFor rel01.1 (next):\n- cmd/wc has main.go but NO test file\n- cmd/cat has main.go and cat_test.go\n- cmd/sponge has NO code at all\n\nSince I can only propose 1 task, I need to pick the most important next step.\n\nGiven the dependency ordering rules:\n1. Libraries before consumers\n2. Implementation before tests\n3. Earlier releases first\n\nSince rel01.0 appears to have code already (ts + testutils), the next logical step would be to work on rel01.1.\n\nFor rel01.1, the dependencies are:\n- wc needs a test file (main.go exists)\n- cat has both main.go and test\n- sponge has nothing\n\nFollowing the priority rules, I need to decide between writing wc's tests or implementing sponge. Since wc's implementation already exists, its tests should come next before starting a completely new implementation like sponge. Looking at the status of each utility, cat is already complete, wc has its implementation but needs tests, and sponge needs both. The wc test is the logical next step since it finishes an in-progress utility. Before committing to that though, I should verify what's actually blocking rel01.0—the ts use case is marked in_progress with code already written, so I'm wondering if there's something else needed there that I'm missing.\n\nAfter reviewing the constraints, I realize tasks need to be independently executable, so I can't just ask for \"run tests and fix failures.\" The wc test file makes the most sense as the next task: it's part of rel01.1, the implementation already exists, the test specification is defined, and it follows the same pattern as the cat and ts test files. I'll create a task to implement the differential tests for wc according to the test specification. Looking at the test-rel01.1.yaml wc test cases:\n- wc_default_three_lines\n- wc_lines_only\n- wc_words_only\n- wc_bytes_only\n- wc_chars_lc_c\n- wc_max_line_length\n- wc_combined_flags_order\n- wc_multi_file_total\n- wc_total_only\n- wc_total_never\n- wc_stdin_dash\n- wc_empty_stdin\n- wc_missing_file\n\nThat's 13 test cases, which would be roughly 200-300 lines following the cat_test.go pattern. I need to cover the requirements from prd005-wc (R1 through R6) and prd001-testutils (R1-R3). Looking at how cat_test.go and ts_test.go are structured, I can see the pattern: TestMain builds the binary and locates the reference, tests use testutils.DiffTest with file fixtures in t.TempDir(), and baseEnv sets LC_ALL=C. Now I'll write the differential test file for wc following this established pattern. _ALL=C environment variable for all tests, and I'm settling on the design approach: following the TestMain pattern from the cat tests, using testutils.RunDiffTests for execution, creating temporary fixtures for multi-file cases, and relying on gwc as the reference binary since wc output is deterministic. Now I need to verify this is actually the right next task by checking if rel01.0 has any incomplete work that should take priority.\n\nLooking at the artifacts, rel01.0 seems complete—testutils, ts code, and ts tests all exist, so the \"in_progress\" status likely just means the tests haven't been validated against the reference binary yet. That means moving forward with rel01.1 makes sense, and wc_test.go is the logical next step since wc/main.go already exists.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":103447,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":103447},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a36ec9c-fdab-4cee-891f-c1eb7b4bdf2c","uuid":"96d2b463-ec56-4d34-979e-e1949a0837a8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CKXujFxfG8ctmdPAbb19RN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven pipeline that regenerates Unix utilities in Go, verified by differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test an AI code generation system (mage-claude-orchestrator) using GNU utilities as subjects.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (PRDs, use cases, test suites).\n\n**Current implementation state**:\n- Code exists: `pkg/testutils` (difftest.go, normalize.go), `cmd/ts` (main.go, ts_test.go), `cmd/cat` (main.go, cat_test.go), `cmd/wc` (main.go only — no test file)\n- Missing code: `cmd/wc` test, `cmd/sponge` (both impl and test), `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/ls`, `cmd/du`\n\n**Current release**: rel01.0 (ts) is in_progress but has code for both implementation and tests. rel01.1 (wc, cat, sponge) is pending — cat is complete (impl + test), wc has implementation but no test, sponge has nothing.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel01.0 has all code artifacts generated. The next actionable work is in rel01.1. Within rel01.1: cat is complete (impl + test exist), wc has implementation but needs its differential test file, and sponge has nothing. Per P8 (implementation before tests for the same feature, but completing a started feature before starting a new one) and P6 (anchor to PRD requirements), the highest-priority task is the wc differential test file.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd005-wc R1-R6, prd001-testutils R1-R3: cmd/wc differential tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd005-wc.yaml (wc requirements R1-R6)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (harness contract R1-R5)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.1.yaml (wc test cases: wc_default_three_lines through wc_missing_file)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (existing wc implementation to be tested)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference pattern for differential test files)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests function, FileExpectation)\n      - pkg/testutils/normalize.go (NormalizeFunc, TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/wc_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Differential tests for cmd/wc exercising all wc test cases from test-rel01.1.yaml\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create cmd/wc/wc_test.go implementing differential tests for all 13 wc test cases defined in test-rel01.1.yaml: wc_default_three_lines, wc_lines_only, wc_words_only, wc_bytes_only, wc_chars_lc_c, wc_max_line_length, wc_combined_flags_order, wc_multi_file_total, wc_total_only, wc_total_never, wc_stdin_dash, wc_empty_stdin, wc_missing_file. Per prd005-wc R1-R6 and prd001-testutils R1-R3.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement TestMain that builds the Go wc binary into a temp directory via 'go build -o <path> .' and locates the Homebrew reference binary gwc via exec.LookPath('gwc'). Follow the exact pattern from cmd/cat/cat_test.go TestMain. Per prd001-testutils R2.1 and sources.yaml (homebrew_binary: gwc).\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement TestWcDifferential that defines a []testutils.DiffTest slice containing all 13 test cases and calls testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests). Skip if goBinary or refBinary are empty. Per prd001-testutils AC1.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"For multi-file test cases (wc_multi_file_total, wc_total_only, wc_total_never, wc_missing_file), create fixture files in t.TempDir() and set DiffTest.WorkDir to the fixture directory. Each fixture file contains the content specified in test-rel01.1.yaml. Per prd001-testutils R2.5.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Set baseEnv to []string{'LC_ALL=C'} and apply it to all test cases. Per test-rel01.1.yaml preconditions and prd005-wc R5.1.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"No normalization is needed for any wc test case -- wc output is deterministic integer counts. Set Normalize to nil on all DiffTest entries. Per test-rel01.1.yaml preconditions.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the TestMain pattern from cmd/cat/cat_test.go exactly: build Go binary to os.MkdirTemp, locate reference via exec.LookPath, defer os.RemoveAll cleanup, exit via os.Exit(m.Run()). The package is 'package main' since this is a cmd/ package.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use testutils.RunDiffTests as the sole test execution mechanism. Do not write standalone unit tests -- all verification is differential per prd001-testutils AC1.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"For file-based tests, create separate t.TempDir() directories per fixture group to avoid cross-contamination. Write fixture files via os.WriteFile with 0644 permissions. Use the file contents exactly as specified in test-rel01.1.yaml.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Reference binary is gwc (Homebrew coreutils, g-prefixed per sources.yaml). Not 'wc' which would be the macOS BSD built-in with different behavior.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"Each DiffTest.Name must match the test case name from test-rel01.1.yaml (e.g., 'wc_default_three_lines') for traceability. Include comments with trace IDs (e.g., 'Traces: prd005-wc R1.1, R1.2, R1.3') matching the pattern in cmd/cat/cat_test.go.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/wc/wc_test.go exists, compiles, and contains exactly 13 DiffTest entries matching the 13 wc test cases in test-rel01.1.yaml.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"TestMain builds the Go wc binary and locates gwc. If either is unavailable, tests skip gracefully via t.Skip.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All multi-file test cases (wc_multi_file_total, wc_total_only, wc_total_never, wc_missing_file) create fixture files in isolated t.TempDir() directories with the exact content specified in test-rel01.1.yaml.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Every DiffTest uses Env: baseEnv (LC_ALL=C) and Normalize: nil.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"'go build ./cmd/wc/...' succeeds with no compilation errors.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"'go vet ./cmd/wc/...' produces no warnings.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":103447,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":103447},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a36ec9c-fdab-4cee-891f-c1eb7b4bdf2c","uuid":"c768eb6c-9c30-46f3-b2d4-c38ec95d30ae"}
